Only the exact-matching library sources and their private/public headers are
vendored. The optional approximate matcher, tools, examples, build system, and
debug allocator are not part of this integration. POSIX ERE matching (including
classes, intervals, alternation, captures, leftmost-longest matching, REG_ICASE,
REG_NOSUB, diagnostics, and deallocation) is implemented by TRE, not translated
to another expression language.

Local changes:
- config.h and include/tre/tre-config.h configure C11, UCRT wide/multibyte and
  character-class functions, malloc-backed matching, and exact matching only.
- lib/tre-internal.h uses uintptr_t instead of long for pointer arithmetic.
- lib/tre-mem.c and lib/tre-match-parallel.c align pointer-bearing data using
  uintptr_t and reserve the matching padding. Windows ARM64 uses LLP64, where
  long is only 32 bits but pointers require 64-bit alignment.
- compat/win32/include/regex.h exposes upstream's POSIX names to ds4 C code.

Case folding and multibyte decoding follow the active C runtime locale, as in
upstream TRE's Windows configuration. The initial C locale is byte-oriented.
Windows wchar_t is UTF-16, so locale-based multibyte character conversion has
the UCRT's wchar_t representability limits; no process-global locale is changed
by this library.

Build exactly these C files, separately (not as an amalgamation):
  third_party/tre/lib/regcomp.c
  third_party/tre/lib/regexec.c
  third_party/tre/lib/regerror.c
  third_party/tre/lib/tre-ast.c
  third_party/tre/lib/tre-compile.c
  third_party/tre/lib/tre-match-backtrack.c
  third_party/tre/lib/tre-match-parallel.c
  third_party/tre/lib/tre-mem.c
  third_party/tre/lib/tre-parse.c
  third_party/tre/lib/tre-stack.c

For clang-cl, add /Ithird_party/tre/include for consumers and these sources.
Force-include /FIthird_party/tre/config.h for only the ten TRE sources above.
Do not define HAVE_CONFIG_H (the configuration is force-included directly).
No external libraries or generated files are required.
